---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ImagineThis.Site | Dan Ryan Neff"
  description="ImagineThis.Site explores imagination as a practical tool for learning, design, entrepreneurship, and building a better future."
>
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-50 via-white to-sky-50 dark:from-gray-900 dark:via-gray-900 dark:to-gray-800">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-6 py-20 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:py-28">

        <div>

          <p class="font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">
            Project
          </p>

          <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white md:text-6xl">
            ImagineThis.Site
          </h1>

          <p class="mt-6 text-2xl leading-relaxed text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            Every meaningful project begins with imagining something that doesn't yet exist.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            ImagineThis.Site is a collection of concepts, thought experiments,
            prototypes, and practical guides exploring how people can create
            better businesses, organizations, communities, and digital experiences.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">

            <a
              href="https://imaginethis.site/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-amber-600 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-amber-700"
            >
              Visit ImagineThis.Site
              <span class="ml-2">↗</span>
            </a>

            <a
              href="/projects/"
              class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 transition hover:bg-white dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-gray-800"
            >
              Back to Projects
            </a>

          </div>

        </div>

        <div>

          <img
            src="/images/DOT_artist_with_ideas.webp"
            alt="An artist surrounded by ideas and creative possibilities"
            class="w-full rounded-2xl shadow-xl"
          />

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Core Idea -->

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20">

      <p class="font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">
        Core idea
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
        Imagination is a practical skill.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">

        <p>
          We often think of imagination as something reserved for artists or
          fiction writers. In reality, nearly every meaningful improvement
          begins by imagining that things could be different.
        </p>

        <p>
          Entrepreneurs imagine businesses that do not yet exist.
          Architects imagine buildings before construction begins.
          Community leaders imagine stronger neighborhoods.
          Technologists imagine new tools.
        </p>

        <p>
          ImagineThis.Site explores that creative process through articles,
          fictional concepts, planning exercises, and practical resources.
        </p>

      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Exploration -->

    <section class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900">

      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">

        <p class="font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">
          Areas of exploration
        </p>

        <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

          <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm dark:bg-gray-800">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Business Ideas</h3>

            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              Imagining organizations that solve problems in thoughtful,
              sustainable ways.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm dark:bg-gray-800">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Technology</h3>

            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              Exploring how AI and digital tools can expand human capability
              instead of replacing human judgment.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm dark:bg-gray-800">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Communities</h3>

            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              Considering how neighborhoods, organizations, and public spaces
              might better support the people who use them.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm dark:bg-gray-800">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Learning</h3>

            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              Curiosity often begins with asking "What if?"
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm dark:bg-gray-800">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Accessibility</h3>

            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              Better design often begins by imagining experiences different
              from our own.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm dark:bg-gray-800">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Everyday Life</h3>

            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
              Sometimes the most meaningful ideas improve ordinary moments
              rather than transform entire industries.
            </p>
          </article>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Why Imagine -->

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">

      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">

        <div>

          <p class="font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">
            Why imagine?
          </p>

          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
            Better questions often come before better answers.
          </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">

          <p>
            Many of the ideas on ImagineThis.Site may never become businesses,
            products, or organizations.
          </p>

          <p>
            That isn't failure.
          </p>

          <p>
            The act of imagining helps clarify values, expose assumptions,
            reveal opportunities, and deepen understanding of how systems work.
          </p>

          <p>
            Even ideas that remain fictional can improve our ability to build
            better real-world solutions.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Quote -->

    <section class="bg-amber-900 text-white">

      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20 text-center">

        <blockquote class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-relaxed md:text-4xl">
          "Imagining better possibilities is one way we discover what is actually possible."
        </blockquote>

      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Why I Built It -->

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20">

      <p class="font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">
        Why I built it
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white md:text-4xl">
        An idea laboratory.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">

        <p>
          Throughout my career I found myself sketching websites,
          organizations, accessibility tools, community projects, business
          concepts, and educational experiences—not because I expected all of
          them to become reality, but because imagining them helped me think
          more clearly.
        </p>

        <p>
          ImagineThis.Site became a place to collect those explorations.
        </p>

        <p>
          Some ideas are practical. Others are ambitious. Some may never leave
          the page. Together they represent a belief that imagination is not
          separate from good judgment—it is one of the ways good judgment
          develops.
        </p>

      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Closing -->

    <section class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900">

      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20 text-center">

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          Explore ImagineThis.Site
        </h2>

        <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          Browse concepts, guides, and thought experiments exploring how
          imagination can shape better technology, organizations, and everyday
          life.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">

          <a
            href="https://imaginethis.site/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-amber-600 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-amber-700"
          >
            Visit ImagineThis.Site
            <span class="ml-2">↗</span>
          </a>

          <a
            href="/projects/"
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 transition hover:bg-white dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-gray-800"
          >
            Back to Projects
          </a>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>